  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.8.2 -- an additive, non-breaking release: a new slider control and a stepper mode for the existing numeric input.\n\nNEW\n- EditRange<T>: an AntDesign-style horizontal slider bound via @bind-Value to any numeric type -- rail, filled track, round handle, optional marks/dots, and a value tooltip. Min/Max resolve param -> [MinValue]/[MaxValue]/[Range] -> 0/100; Step resolves param -> [Step] -> 1. Marks render clickable labeled points; SnapToMarks restricts the value to them; Dots draws step/mark dots (capped at 100); Included (default true) fills the track and styles the active mark. ShowTooltip (default true) shows a value bubble on hover/focus/drag, formatted via TooltipFormat (falls back to [DisplayFormat]) which also drives aria-valuetext and the read-only text. role=\"slider\" track with full keyboard support (arrows/Home/End/PageUp/PageDown); pointer drag via the new lazily-imported wss-slider.js, with a no-JS click fallback and a 24px hit area. Forced-colors and reduced-motion supported. Deliberately excludes vertical/reverse orientation, dual-handle range mode, and an always-open tooltip.\n- EditNumber<T> gains ShowStepper (bool, default false): renders a minus/plus button pair around the input, stepping by the effective Step (param -> model [Step] -> 1), clamped to EffectiveMin/EffectiveMax; buttons auto-disable at the bounds and when the control is disabled. Native spinners hide while the mode is on. DecreaseButtonLabel/IncreaseButtonLabel override the accessible names (default \"Decrease {label}\"/\"Increase {label}\"). Buttons are not tab stops -- keyboard users step via the input's native arrows -- and there is no press-and-hold auto-repeat. Off by default; the stepper-off DOM is byte-identical to 10.8.1.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog",
